From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 07:44:42 +0200
Subject: Do not recover inline-proxy skolems in avoidance under capture
 checking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream #26563 (3.9.0-RC5) typed the proxy for an unstable argument to a
dependent inline method with the typer-minted SkolemType; #26872 reverted that
to the widened argument type and instead records the skolem on the proxy
binding so type avoidance can substitute it into the expansion's type. Under
capture checking that substitution is still wrong: the skolem-mentioning
expansion type cannot be avoided into a pure declared result, so derivation
results summoned via summonFrom fail with "capability `typeclass` cannot flow
into capture set {}". Not planting the attachment in cc-enabled units restores
plain widening avoidance — the behaviour every cc unit had before RC5 — while
leaving the #26153/#26031/#26810 fix active elsewhere; upstream's own
regression tests for those still pass.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude); the capture-mode failure has a
standalone reproduction in the feature documentation, and the need for the
gate was established by building the full Soundness tree on this commit's
base with and without it.

Proscala-Patch: proxyskolem
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inliner.scala | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inliner.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inliner.scala
index 581371f902e2f9fb206804dd9a9421def64bac3a..5c0cc6aeb18de07b8f59240365a34ca68342f8c6 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inliner.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inliner.scala
@@ -356,7 +356,12 @@ class Inliner(val call: tpd.Tree)(using Context):
       if isByName then DefDef(boundSym, newArg)
       else ValDef(boundSym, newArg)
     }.withSpan(boundSym.span)
-    if !argIsBottom then // Record typer skolem on the proxy ValDef, so the `avoidingType` can avoid proxy to skolem.
+    // Under capture checking, do not record the skolem: avoid-time recovery substitutes it
+    // into the expansion's type, where cc's Fresh roots cannot absorb it — a summoned
+    // capability-typed instance can then never flow back into a pure declared result
+    // (upstream #26563's capture-mode casualties). Plain widening avoidance, as before
+    // #26563, is what every cc unit had; non-cc units keep the #26153/#26031/#26810 fix.
+    if !argIsBottom && !config.Feature.ccEnabled then // Record typer skolem on the proxy ValDef, so the `avoidingType` can avoid proxy to skolem.
       skolem.foreach(binding.putAttachment(TypeAssigner.InlineProxySkolem, _))
       // Or, if the argument's own type is already some other skolem (generated by some external call), record that separately.
       if skolem.isEmpty then
